  "hinge": "The cause is not the selloff and not the data centre; it is the deal structure in which a company takes a square mile, 782 generators and a share of the grid, and the people who live there receive the residue. §4:98 is unusually exact about this: profit taken from a counterparty without friendship is described as plunder, and the same verse gives the practical consequence — \"you cannot achieve any friendship between that human being and yourselves\", which is the sentence a permitting hearing writes in its own words. The reversal is cheap relative to the capex already committed: generation built and paid for on site, water metered and returned, an abatement schedule published, a community agreement with a term. None of that is a moratorium, and all of it is the difference between a deal and an extraction."
